cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  CBF-LMM: Conditional Bayes-Factor Selection with an Adaptive
  Polygenic Background
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the manuscript and the
  software itself using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Doulabe
    given-names: "Kossi N."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6317-5654"
    affiliation: >-
      Département de Mathématiques et de Statistique, Université Laval,
      Québec, Canada
  - family-names: Lakhal-Chaieb
    given-names: "Lajmi"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8358-4392"
    affiliation: >-
      Département de Mathématiques et de Statistique, Université Laval,
      Québec, Canada
abstract: >-
  CBF-LMM is a conditional Bayes-factor stepwise procedure for
  refining candidate regions under an adaptive linear mixed-model
  polygenic background that excludes the candidate under
  evaluation.  At
  each step the candidate-specific marginal likelihood integrates the
  residual variance analytically and the variance-component ratio is
  numerically marginalised by one-dimensional Gauss-Legendre
  quadrature; model growth is controlled by a profile-maximum-likelihood
  extended BIC on the full accepted model.  The
  conditional Bayes factor recovers Wakefield's approximate Bayes
  factor asymptotically in the residual degrees of freedom.  A plug-in REML evaluation of the
  variance-component ratio and a posterior-score stopping rule are
  provided as sensitivity options, and an exploratory joint
  Schur-complement score is retained for future development.
keywords:
  - "Bayesian variable selection"
  - "linear mixed model"
  - "Bayes factor"
  - "genetic fine-mapping"
  - "polygenic background"
  - "stepwise selection"
  - "extended BIC"
  - "Gauss-Legendre quadrature"
